                  "value": "PARTIAL",
                  "description": "The type of search to be performed, partial or full. If PARTIAL is requested, a partial match of search criteria will return the party. If FULL is requested, the whole keyword must match the search criteria to return the customer. \n\nPARTIAL: Returns results where the party attribute starts with or contains the search criteria. For example, searching for a postalCode of \"338\" returns all parties with postal codes beginning with \"338\" (e.g., 33801, 33813). Searching for addressLine1 of \"LAKE\" returns all parties with street name within the address line 1 containing \"LAKE\" (e.g., 98 LAKE BYRD BLVD, 2851 S LAKE LETTA DR, 947 LAKE ANGELO DR, 2720 LAKEVIEW DR). Searching for city of \"LAKE\" returns all parties with city names beginning with \"LAKE\" (e.g. LAKE GENEVA, LAKE PARK, LAKE PLACID). Partial matching applies to:\n\n  * addressLine1\n  * postalAddressCity\n  * postalCode\n  * firstName\n  * organizationName\n\nWhen searching for a person (partyType = \"PERSON\"), the person is returned if the first name begins with the value supplied for firstName and the last name is an exact match. For instance, if the firstName is \"JOE\" and lastName is \"SMITH\", then both JOEL SMITH and JOE SMITH are returned in the response. However, the party with first name JOE and last name SMITHSON would not be returned, since the last name must be an exact match regardless of the searchType. When searching for an organization (partyType = \"ORGANIZATION\"), the organization is returned if the organization name begins with the value supplied for organizationName. For instance, if searching with organizationName of \"SMITH\", then all organizations that begin with SMITH are returned (e.g., SMITH AUTO LLC, SMITH CAR WASH LLC, SMITH ENTERPRISES, SMITH LAWN SERVICE). The postalAddressStateProvince must be an exact match regardess of the partyType. \n\nFULL: Returns results only when the keyword is an exact match for the party data.\n\nThe valid values are available from the retrievePersonControls API, searchTypeValidValues[].searchType. \n\nThe search type qualifier is not applicable when searching with tax identifier (taxIdentifier)."
